{"running": "Lesson Eighteen", "pages": [{"src": [60], "blocks": [{"t": "lesson", "n": 18, "title": "Lesson Eighteen", "sub": "Eighteenth (18th) Lesson"}, {"t": "part", "n": "I", "title": "“Dialogue”"}, {"t": "inst", "text": "Claudia and Louis are talking in the zoo. They are talking about the animals. Listen:"}, {"t": "olist", "num": false, "items": ["*C –* Do you see how the animals are eating?", "*L –* Yes, I can see them. Look over there!", "*C –* What happens?", "*L –* It’s so funny to see the female monkey feeding the little monkey.", "*C –* Oh, yes, I had never seen that. It’s very curious.", "*L –* Let’s take some photos.", "*C –* Good idea!"]}, {"t": "h", "text": "Write a similar dialogue"}, {"t": "write", "num": false, "rowGap": "8px", "items": [{"q": ""}, {"q": ""}, {"q": ""}, {"q": ""}, {"q": ""}, {"q": ""}, {"q": ""}, {"q": ""}, {"q": ""}]}]}, {"src": [60, 61], "blocks": [{"t": "h", "text": "Mark the corresponding letter according with the color of the animal:"}, {"t": "img", "src": "img/v/l18-colors1.svg", "h": "175px"}, {"t": "img", "src": "img/v/l18-colors2.svg", "h": "175px"}, {"t": "img", "src": "img/v/l18-colors3.svg", "h": "175px"}]}, {"src": [61], "blocks": [{"t": "h", "text": "“Some Other Animals” in Alphabetical Order"}, {"t": "pairs", "rows": [["*A)* Ant – Antelope", "*K)* Kangaroo"], ["*B)* Bee – Bull – Bird", "*L)* Lizard – Lobster – Lamb"], ["*C)* Camel – Cat – Cricket", "*M)* Mosquito – Mouse – Moth"], ["*D)* Dog – Donkey – Dove", "*O)* Owl – Ostrich"], ["*E)* Eagle – Elephant", "*P)* Panther – Parrot – Pig – Penguin"], ["*F)* Fly – Frog – Fish", "*R)* Rabbit – Rat – Rooster"], ["*G)* Giraffe – Goose – Grasshopper", "*S)* Seal – Sea horse – Snake – Shark – Sheep – Swan"], ["*H)* Horse – Hippopotamus", "*T)* Turtle – Turkey – Toad"], ["*I)* Insects (many kinds of them)", "*W)* Whale – Wolf – Wasp – Woodpecker"], ["", "*Z)* Zebra."]]}]}, {"src": [62], "blocks": [{"t": "part", "n": "II", "title": "“In Grammar Class” — Present perfect continuous…"}, {"t": "olist", "items": ["I *have been watching* T.V. all night long.", "You *have been renting* a big flat.", "She *has been speaking* in French.", "He *has been shaving* himself.", "We *have been doing* the housework.", "You *have been reading* that magazine.", "They *have been seeing* those girls."]}, {"t": "h", "text": "“Interrogative Form”"}, {"t": "note", "text": "Have you been watching T.V. all night long?"}, {"t": "h", "text": "Full answers:"}, {"t": "olist", "num": false, "items": ["*+* Yes, I have been watching T.V. all night long.", "*–* No, I haven’t been watching T.V. all night long."]}, {"t": "h", "text": "Short sentences:"}, {"t": "olist", "num": false, "items": ["Yes, I have. — No, I haven’t."]}, {"t": "write", "num": false, "rowGap": "6px", "qw": "110px", "items": [{"q": "2. Have"}, {"q": "Yes,"}, {"q": "3. Has"}, {"q": "No,"}, {"q": "4. Has"}, {"q": "Yes,"}, {"q": "5. Have"}, {"q": "No,"}, {"q": "6. Have"}, {"q": "Yes,"}, {"q": "7. Have"}, {"q": "No,"}]}]}]}